    "body": "Done. Merged to develop as 561bd71ea5e4e142411d105a7f041bc866a936f7.\n\nImplemented the full data layer foundation: Postgres schema (databases/properties/relation_definitions/items partitioned by database_id/item_relations/project_heartbeats/agent_runs/resource_grants/rollup_dependencies/notifications/users), the generic choke-point CRUD service enforcing locked/schema_locked/owner with Idempotency-Key + ifVersion optimistic concurrency, eager property-type migration (idempotent under graphile-worker retries), the SchedulerStore heartbeat module (5 rule kinds, DST-safe via Luxon, FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED sweep, onItemEvent write-path trigger), the rollup engine (config validation, mirror lifecycle checks, 3 trigger events, backfill that doesn't hold a pool connection across its full walk), packages/queue on graphile-worker, the permission manifest + drift-check heartbeat, owner_process orphan detection, the agent_runs delegation model with core.agentRun as an injectable stub, and the Semp/Semprec system seed (System settings + Projects, both schema-locked).\n\nNotes for dependent issues:\n- The choke-point's public store functions (propertiesStore/itemsStore/databasesStore/relationsStore) are intentionally NOT re-exported from the package's index.ts barrel — only their input types are. Go through `createChokePoint()`.\n- `computedKeyRegistry.ts` (a Set<string> of declared module cache keys, same temporary-stub pattern as ActionRegistry) already guards property creation against colliding with a future module's computed key; issue #29 populates it.\n- CI-layer import ban (dependency-cruiser) and Postgres role separation (semprec_data/semprec_side) are issue #40's scope, not this one — see the PR discussion for the exact quotes from #40's spec justifying that split.\n- This PR went through 8 review rounds; a real infra bug was found and fixed along the way (code-review-bot's own file-fetch script crashed on this PR's diff size — see the code-review-bot repo, commit 0a8279e).",
